From 5ce5dee3efca33140de830d22c575b6732bce9b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JimmyBlunt <jo@paso-music.de>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:05:07 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] Edit FastLED Patterns as C++ in the Studio editor
 (local #9002)

Same Editor/Monaco surface, editorFlavor stays 'pattern'; the language is
derived from the buffer's marker.

- PixelblazeCodeEditor: `language` prop, FastLED buffers use Monaco's
  built-in `cpp`; registers FastLED completion/hover (static catalogue in
  engine/fastled/fastledApiCatalog.ts: FastLED.*, CRGB members and named
  colours, lib8tion, colour utilities, palettes, timing macros, UISlider/
  UICheckbox/UINumberField, PXLBLZ_NUM_LEDS).
- Editor: FastLED buffers skip the Pixelblaze validator and request an
  async compile; compiler diagnostics become Monaco markers (owner
  'fastled') for the exact buffer only; the Pixelblaze debounce never
  publishes FastLED source. Unmarked `#include <FastLED.h>` C++ gets an
  explicit "Convert to FastLED Pattern" action (prepends the marker).
- CompileStatusBadge pulses (working tone) while the buffer compiles.
- openPatternRecord: FastLED source is published provisionally (the
  preview compiles it; a failure makes it unavailable and broken).
- Navigation preflight judges FastLED drafts by compileStatus, not by the
  Pixelblaze parser.

Pre-commit hook checks run manually (hook cannot spawn npx.cmd on Windows/Node 24):
npm run lint, check:e2e-coverage, check:e2e-locators, tsc -b (tsconfig + node),
vitest Editor.fastled + Editor.recovery + fastledProviders + openPattern +
navigationPreflightStore (43 passed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
